---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Axon Fusus | Providers | NoRec.US"
  description="Axon Fusus real-time crime center and sensor-fusion platform, documented Illinois licensing, and official product information."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell provider_detail">
  <header class="article_header provider_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROVIDER / PLATFORM</p>
    <h1>Axon Fusus</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Real-time crime center software that combines live video, alerts, location data, ALPR overlays, and other public-safety data into a common operational interface.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">OWNERSHIP</p>
    <h2>Fusus is part of Axon</h2>
    <p>Axon acquired Fusus in February 2024. NoRec keeps a separate Fusus page because contracts and agency records may identify the Fusus platform by name even though the product now belongs to Axon.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTED ILLINOIS RELATIONSHIP</p>
    <h2>DeKalb Police Department</h2>
    <div class="provider_evidence_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Fusus user licensing</h3>
        <p>DeKalb's 2025 Axon agreement includes Axon Fusus “Plus User” licenses as part of the department's five-year Axon program beginning in 2026.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">SCOPE</span>
        <h3>Licensing does not establish every integration</h3>
        <p>The agreement establishes access to Fusus licensing. It does not by itself prove which private cameras, public cameras, CAD feeds, ALPR systems, sensors, or other integrations are currently connected.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PUBLISHED PRODUCT CAPABILITIES</p>
    <h2>What Axon says Fusus can combine</h2>
    <div class="provider_capability_grid">
      <article><h3>Live video</h3><p>Axon describes Fusus as combining public and private video streams in a unified real-time interface.</p></article>
      <article><h3>ALPR and vehicle information</h3><p>Axon's current product material describes ALPR overlays and vehicle identification/tracking within the platform.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Dispatch and field data</h3><p>Axon describes officer location, alerts, dispatch information, and other operational data appearing on a shared live map.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Sensor fusion</h3><p>Official material describes integrations with cameras, drones, IoT sources, floor plans, gunshot-detection triggers, and other feeds.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / GOVERNANCE</p>
    <h2>The platform is defined by what gets connected</h2>
    <div class="provider_questions">
      <details><summary>Private-camera access</summary><p>Axon says Fusus can incorporate privately owned camera feeds with permission. Whether an Illinois agency has such feeds connected requires agency-specific evidence.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Role-based access</summary><p>Axon's product documentation describes configurable role-based access. Local permissions and user counts should be established from agency records.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Retention</summary><p>A real-time integration platform can expose multiple underlying systems with different retention rules. NoRec should document retention at the source system as well as any export or evidence workflow.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Audit and disclosure</summary><p>Contracts, access logs, integration inventories, camera-sharing agreements, user roles, and audit records are key records for determining the practical scope of a deployment.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="official_product_links">
    <p class="eyebrow">VENDOR DOCUMENTATION</p>
    <h2>Official product information</h2>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.axon.com/products/axon-fusus" rel="external">Axon Fusus — official product page</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.axon.com/products/axon-fusus/unified-interface" rel="external">Axon Fusus — unified interface</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://investor.axon.com/2024-02-01-Axon-Accelerates-Real-Time-Operations-Solution-with-Strategic-Acquisition-of-Fusus" rel="external">Axon — 2024 Fusus acquisition announcement</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS RECORDS</p>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="/county/60178/">DeKalb County jurisdiction file</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cityofdekalb.com/DocumentCenter/View/19825/Res-2025-085-Passed-092225-Axon" rel="external">City of DeKalb — 2025 Axon agreement</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
